menu "Firefly EasyTouch Capture"

    config FIREFLY_EASYTOUCH_PASSWORD
        string "Micro-Air account password"
        default ""
        help
            The password of the Micro-Air account already paired to the
            coach's EasyTouch thermostat (the same one the phone app uses
            to connect over Bluetooth). This is the ONLY credential the
            protocol uses -- there is no separate BLE pairing. See
            docs/EASYTOUCH-THERMOSTAT.md section 2.

            Set this in THIS project's own sdkconfig only
            (hvac_capture/sdkconfig) -- never in sdkconfig.defaults, same
            handling as every other real secret in this repo (battery MACs,
            ESP-NOW peer MAC/PMK/LMK).

    config FIREFLY_EASYTOUCH_EMAIL
        string "Micro-Air account e-mail (optional)"
        default ""
        help
            Sent as the "EM" field on a Get Status request if non-empty.
            The design's recommendation (docs/EASYTOUCH-THERMOSTAT.md
            section 3.3) is to leave this and the timestamp out, since the
            thermostat sets its clock from a connecting app's timestamp and
            this capture tool has no clock to give it. Leave blank unless
            bench step 2 (status with vs. without EM/TM) needs to compare.

    config FIREFLY_EASYTOUCH_NAME_PREFIX
        string "Advertised name prefix to scan for"
        default "EasyTouch"
        help
            The thermostat advertises as "EasyTouch <serial>". Prefix match
            is fine for a single thermostat in range.

    config FIREFLY_EASYTOUCH_POLL_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Status poll interval (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 2000 60000
        help
            Bench-capture cadence, deliberately fast (not the eventual
            gateway's 20-30 s production interval) so a mode change made on
            the touchscreen shows up in the log quickly during a capture
            session.

endmenu
